{
  "source": "course-assets/where-will-ai-land/where-will-ai-land.mp4",
  "duration": 204.9493125,
  "segments": [
    {
      "start": 0.0,
      "end": 5.72,
      "text": "Right now, you can find thousands of tech experts making incredibly confident, hyper-specific"
    },
    {
      "start": 5.72,
      "end": 9.66,
      "text": "predictions about exactly where artificial intelligence is heading."
    },
    {
      "start": 10.14,
      "end": 13.0,
      "text": "The best way to see it is a true story about rats."
    },
    {
      "start": 13.9,
      "end": 17.6,
      "text": "In 1902, the city of Hanoi was rapidly modernizing."
    },
    {
      "start": 18.18,
      "end": 22.06,
      "text": "The colonial government laid down miles of new, state-of-the-art sewer pipes."
    },
    {
      "start": 22.8,
      "end": 27.76,
      "text": "Unfortunately, those dark, protected tunnels provided the perfect breeding ground for"
    },
    {
      "start": 27.76,
      "end": 29.68,
      "text": "a massive rat infestation."
    },
    {
      "start": 30.22,
      "end": 32.88,
      "text": "City officials devised what looked like a mathematically"
    },
    {
      "start": 32.88,
      "end": 33.96,
      "text": "flawless solution."
    },
    {
      "start": 34.72,
      "end": 37.22,
      "text": "They created a bounty system, offering citizens"
    },
    {
      "start": 37.22,
      "end": 40.94,
      "text": "a small cash payment for every severed rat tail handed in."
    },
    {
      "start": 41.42,
      "end": 43.42,
      "text": "Initially, the metrics looked phenomenal."
    },
    {
      "start": 43.94,
      "end": 46.6,
      "text": "Tails poured into government offices by the thousands"
    },
    {
      "start": 46.6,
      "end": 47.64,
      "text": "on a daily basis."
    },
    {
      "start": 48.18,
      "end": 49.98,
      "text": "But shortly after the program launched,"
    },
    {
      "start": 50.54,
      "end": 53.04,
      "text": "citizens started noticing healthy, completely"
    },
    {
      "start": 53.04,
      "end": 55.68,
      "text": "tailless rats scurrying around the city streets."
    },
    {
      "start": 55.68,
      "end": 58.44,
      "text": "The math had a biological loophole."
    },
    {
      "start": 59.14,
      "end": 61.84,
      "text": "A rat can survive perfectly fine without its tail."
    },
    {
      "start": 62.42,
      "end": 65.72,
      "text": "And more importantly, it can keep making more rat babies."
    },
    {
      "start": 66.48,
      "end": 70.48,
      "text": "The rat hunters figured out that killing the animal destroyed their own supply chain."
    },
    {
      "start": 70.96,
      "end": 74.38,
      "text": "So they caught the rats, clipped the tails to collect the cash,"
    },
    {
      "start": 74.74,
      "end": 77.22,
      "text": "and released them back into the sewers to breed."
    },
    {
      "start": 78.0,
      "end": 79.22,
      "text": "A dead rat pays once."
    },
    {
      "start": 79.82,
      "end": 82.08,
      "text": "A live rat pays forever."
    },
    {
      "start": 82.08,
      "end": 91.7,
      "text": "Some local entrepreneurs realized hunting wild rats was too much work, so they bypassed the sewers entirely and set up dedicated rat breeding farms."
    },
    {
      "start": 92.64,
      "end": 96.6,
      "text": "The government eventually caught onto the scam and completely scrapped the bounty program."
    },
    {
      "start": 97.02,
      "end": 106.84,
      "text": "They were left with a literal mountain of severed tails in their offices, but the actual living rat population in Hanoi was significantly higher than before the bounty started."
    },
    {
      "start": 106.84,
      "end": 109.74,
      "text": "But the real goal was fewer rats,"
    },
    {
      "start": 110.1,
      "end": 112.68,
      "text": "and the program encouraged people to keep rats alive."
    },
    {
      "start": 113.4,
      "end": 115.1,
      "text": "Hanoi's plan was fewer rats."
    },
    {
      "start": 115.56,
      "end": 117.88,
      "text": "The unexpected result was more rats."
    },
    {
      "start": 118.36,
      "end": 119.92,
      "text": "Here are two more unexpected results,"
    },
    {
      "start": 120.4,
      "end": 123.2,
      "text": "one welcome surprise and one costly mistake."
    },
    {
      "start": 123.8,
      "end": 125.72,
      "text": "First, look at SMS text messaging."
    },
    {
      "start": 126.38,
      "end": 129.96,
      "text": "It was originally built strictly to send short, utilitarian messages"
    },
    {
      "start": 129.96,
      "end": 131.46,
      "text": "over early mobile networks."
    },
    {
      "start": 131.98,
      "end": 134.82,
      "text": "Its creators did not expect it to be a primary feature."
    },
    {
      "start": 134.82,
      "end": 140.98,
      "text": "Instead, young users got hold of the technology and repurposed it, turning texting into a"
    },
    {
      "start": 140.98,
      "end": 143.46,
      "text": "daily, constant way to stay in touch with each other."
    },
    {
      "start": 143.8,
      "end": 147.04,
      "text": "Australia imported cane toads to eat beetles, destroying sugarcane."
    },
    {
      "start": 147.56,
      "end": 151.84,
      "text": "They barely controlled the pests, poisoned native animals, and spread across the country."
    },
    {
      "start": 152.74,
      "end": 157.54,
      "text": "Now, point that historical track record directly at the AI experts making today's"
    },
    {
      "start": 157.54,
      "end": 157.92,
      "text": "headlines."
    },
    {
      "start": 158.3,
      "end": 162.12,
      "text": "Every AI expert working today is making a firm prediction about our future."
    },
    {
      "start": 162.12,
      "end": 167.62,
      "text": "These are smart, well-researched forecasts built on solid data from all camps."
    },
    {
      "start": 168.08,
      "end": 177.08,
      "text": "The most important thing AI does in your lifetime, good or bad, may be something nobody in any camp, any lab, or any course has thought of yet."
    },
    {
      "start": 177.52,
      "end": 183.24,
      "text": "That's not a reason to fear the future. It's the reason to walk into it curious, with your eyes open."
    },
    {
      "start": 183.9,
      "end": 186.28,
      "text": "You do not need to predict the future perfectly."
    },
    {
      "start": 186.28,
      "end": 191.76,
      "text": "You need to recognize uncertainty, watch what people actually do, and build skills"
    },
    {
      "start": 191.76,
      "end": 194.0,
      "text": "that still matter when the forecast changes."
    },
    {
      "start": 194.64,
      "end": 199.44,
      "text": "As this final text banner highlights, some of the biggest results are the ones nobody"
    },
    {
      "start": 199.44,
      "end": 199.92,
      "text": "predicted."
    },
    {
      "start": 200.48,
      "end": 202.58,
      "text": "That's the best reason to stay curious."
    }
  ],
